WEBVTT

00:00:04.690 --> 00:00:07.110
Beginning today, our enemy is

00:00:07.110 --> 00:00:08.980
Nobunaga Oda!

00:00:08.980 --> 00:00:13.650
<i>With Nagamasa Azai's unbelievable betrayal,
Saburo is put in a tight situation.</i>

00:00:14.640 --> 00:00:20.700
<i>But with the success of Hideyoshi and 
his men, they manage to make it to Kyoto.</i>

00:00:22.000 --> 00:00:24.040
We'll fight Azai, and win.

00:00:24.680 --> 00:00:28.560
I have to conquer Japan, after all.

00:00:28.560 --> 00:00:32.510
<i>But that was just the beginning 
of a thorny road.</i>

00:00:34.230 --> 00:00:35.010
My lord.

00:00:35.990 --> 00:00:37.300
Hey, Kyu-chan!

00:00:37.570 --> 00:00:39.060
Saburo's assistant,

00:00:39.910 --> 00:00:41.430
Hidemasa Hori.

00:00:41.430 --> 00:00:43.420
Commonly known as Kyutaro.

00:00:43.860 --> 00:00:46.150
Takenaka-dono has arrived.

00:00:46.400 --> 00:00:48.650
Great! Is Hanbei-chan back?

00:00:50.180 --> 00:00:52.070
Omi, the Kamaha Castle lord,

00:00:52.070 --> 00:00:56.660
and Hori Hidemura have declared 
that they are betraying you.

00:00:56.660 --> 00:00:59.990
I believe the path is now clear for 
punitive action against the Azai family.

00:00:59.990 --> 00:01:02.040
Yep. Thanks, Hanbei-chan.

00:01:02.040 --> 00:01:02.950
Good work.

00:01:03.410 --> 00:01:06.170
So you had ordered 
Takenaka-dono to strategize.

00:01:06.630 --> 00:01:07.930
Yep.

00:01:07.930 --> 00:01:10.500
Then, my lord, we are finally —

00:01:11.180 --> 00:01:12.030
Yep.

00:01:12.950 --> 00:01:14.380
We're moving out.

00:01:23.180 --> 00:01:24.930
<b>Episode 9</b>

00:01:23.180 --> 00:01:24.930
<b>A Thorny Road</b>

00:01:25.800 --> 00:01:27.940
Odani Castle, huh?

00:01:28.320 --> 00:01:31.110
That whole mountain 
is a castle, isn't it?

00:01:31.110 --> 00:01:34.650
People in the Warring States period 
sure were impressive.

00:01:34.650 --> 00:01:38.840
They've gone and carved out a mountain to 
build a castle, without machines or anything.

00:01:38.840 --> 00:01:41.830
Why are you so impressed, 
all of a sudden?

00:01:41.830 --> 00:01:45.370
My lord, it will be difficult 
to take that castle.

00:01:45.880 --> 00:01:49.880
Yeah, attacking it now 
wouldn't work.

00:01:52.940 --> 00:01:55.930
The Oda army is over there, correct?

00:01:55.930 --> 00:01:56.960
Yes.

00:02:01.340 --> 00:02:04.340
Brother!

00:02:11.060 --> 00:02:12.540
Oi-cchan?

00:02:12.540 --> 00:02:13.670
What?

00:02:13.670 --> 00:02:16.940
I thought I heard 
Oi-cchan calling me.

00:02:19.630 --> 00:02:22.600
Do you want to return 
to your brother, Oichi?

00:02:25.490 --> 00:02:26.450
My lord!

00:02:26.720 --> 00:02:29.530
There's a fire in the castle town!

00:02:32.620 --> 00:02:35.250
They're trying to lure me 
out of the castle.

00:02:35.650 --> 00:02:38.340
Nagamasa-dono, let us surrender.

00:02:39.210 --> 00:02:40.760
Wait here, Oichi.

00:02:41.780 --> 00:02:46.180
This is the war in which I will finally 
bring home Nobunaga's head.

00:02:46.950 --> 00:02:48.230
I don't want that!

00:02:50.510 --> 00:02:53.980
My lord, there is no sign that 
Azai will leave the castle.

00:02:54.550 --> 00:02:56.890
So he cannot be lured out.

00:02:58.200 --> 00:02:59.180
All right.

00:02:59.940 --> 00:03:00.700
New plan.

00:03:02.820 --> 00:03:04.430
Let's go to Yokoyama Castle.

00:03:05.190 --> 00:03:08.280
<i>Saburo, having quickly 
given up fighting in Odani,</i>

00:03:05.450 --> 00:03:12.120
<b>Lake Biwa</b>

00:03:05.450 --> 00:03:12.120
<b>Oda army</b>

00:03:05.450 --> 00:03:12.120
<b>Toragoze Mountain</b>

00:03:05.450 --> 00:03:12.120
<b>Odani Castle</b>

00:03:05.450 --> 00:03:12.120
<b>Ane River</b>

00:03:05.450 --> 00:03:12.120
<b>Yokoyama Castle</b>

00:03:08.280 --> 00:03:12.120
<i>instead surrounds Azai's precious 
fortress of Yokoyama Castle.</i>

00:03:13.630 --> 00:03:17.290
My lord, Yokoyama Castle 
is under attack!

00:03:17.290 --> 00:03:18.670
We must send help.

00:03:18.670 --> 00:03:21.680
We will at a severe disadvantage 
if we lose it.

00:03:22.500 --> 00:03:26.220
We must wait for Yoshikage Asakura-dono's
 support forces.

00:03:26.220 --> 00:03:29.680
We cannot afford to lose 
a single man in vain.

00:03:30.360 --> 00:03:32.720
We just need a little patience.

00:03:32.720 --> 00:03:34.930
The time will surely come.

00:03:37.140 --> 00:03:40.070
My lord, Asakura-sama has arrived.

00:03:41.060 --> 00:03:45.610
I'm the Asakura army's supreme general,
 Kagitake Asakura.

00:03:45.610 --> 00:03:48.870
I have come from Echizen 
with 10,000 men.

00:03:49.510 --> 00:03:52.760
I was hoping Yoshikage-dono 
would come, but it seems...

00:03:52.760 --> 00:03:56.880
My lord, Yoshikage, has left me 
in charge of this army.

00:03:57.570 --> 00:04:00.590
Let us fight together 
with all our might.

00:04:00.950 --> 00:04:05.640
<i>Meanwhile, support forces have been 
arriving on Saburo's side, as well.</i>

00:04:06.260 --> 00:04:09.470
Hey! You came, Ieyasu-kun!

00:04:10.540 --> 00:04:14.810
Yes. I have but 5,000 men,
but I hope they will be of some help.

00:04:15.280 --> 00:04:16.640
Thanks.

00:04:16.640 --> 00:04:19.960
The Mikawa people are strong, 
so this is reassuring.

00:04:19.960 --> 00:04:22.440
Thank you for your kind words.

00:04:22.440 --> 00:04:27.040
But why has Asakura's lord not come?

00:04:27.040 --> 00:04:29.640
Oda is an enemy to both of us.

00:04:29.640 --> 00:04:32.220
We are equally invested 
in this battle.

00:04:32.940 --> 00:04:34.730
It can't be helped. 
He's not coming.

00:04:35.170 --> 00:04:36.560
Kazumasa...

00:04:36.580 --> 00:04:38.030
Naotsune...

00:04:38.680 --> 00:04:40.660
We are counting on you.

00:04:41.090 --> 00:04:43.930
Take Nobunaga's head, no matter what!

00:04:43.930 --> 00:04:44.990
Yes, sir!

00:04:45.310 --> 00:04:48.570
<i>And so the Azai and Asakura armies</i>

00:04:45.970 --> 00:04:50.640
<b>Yokoyama Castle</b>

00:04:45.970 --> 00:04:50.640
<b>Tokugawa army</b>

00:04:45.970 --> 00:04:50.640
<b>Oda army</b>

00:04:45.970 --> 00:04:50.640
<b>Ane River</b>

00:04:45.970 --> 00:04:50.640
<b>Oui Mountain</b>

00:04:45.970 --> 00:04:50.640
<b>Asakura army</b>

00:04:45.970 --> 00:04:50.640
<b>Asai army</b>

00:04:45.970 --> 00:04:50.640
<b>Odani 
Castle</b>

00:04:48.570 --> 00:04:50.190
<i>took up position at Oumi Mountain.</i>

00:04:50.640 --> 00:04:53.770
<i>At last, they appeared 
in front of the Oda army.</i>

00:04:54.600 --> 00:04:57.710
There he is: Nagamasa Azai!

00:04:59.040 --> 00:05:01.520
He's too far to see clearly, but yeah.

00:05:01.520 --> 00:05:04.950
So Azai was waiting for 
Asakura's support.

00:05:06.160 --> 00:05:09.250
All right, we'll have to hold off 
on our attack on Yokoyama Castle

00:05:09.250 --> 00:05:10.780
and bring everyone back.

00:05:11.700 --> 00:05:17.440
We're too spread thin to fight,
so we'd better get in formation soon.

00:05:17.440 --> 00:05:21.960
Otherwise this army will end up 
on the front lines, with you in it.

00:05:22.540 --> 00:05:24.290
I know, right?

00:05:24.290 --> 00:05:25.590
That would suck.

00:05:30.010 --> 00:05:31.640
My lord! My lord!

00:05:33.280 --> 00:05:33.930
What?

00:05:34.370 --> 00:05:36.730
Please leave this place, quickly!

00:05:37.160 --> 00:05:38.650
It's a surprise attack!

00:05:38.650 --> 00:05:40.900
The Azai army crossed the Ane River.

00:05:40.900 --> 00:05:42.980
They're approaching this main army.

00:05:42.980 --> 00:05:45.310
...Whaaaat?!

00:05:45.310 --> 00:05:48.220
Please retreat somewhere safe.

00:05:48.220 --> 00:05:49.970
We'll hold them off here!

00:05:49.970 --> 00:05:51.740
I'm running again?

00:05:57.450 --> 00:05:59.480
Hey, Kyu-chan!

00:05:59.480 --> 00:06:00.440
Yes, sir!

00:06:00.900 --> 00:06:03.110
Is this how Nobunaga is?

00:06:03.610 --> 00:06:04.160
Huh?

00:06:04.160 --> 00:06:07.420
I've always had this, like,

00:06:07.990 --> 00:06:11.650
awesome impression of Nobunaga.

00:06:12.350 --> 00:06:15.000
But I feel like I'm always running lately.

00:06:15.000 --> 00:06:16.420
Man...

00:06:16.770 --> 00:06:20.610
With all due respect, it doesn't matter 
whether you look awesome or not.

00:06:20.610 --> 00:06:24.880
The winner in this troubled world 
is the one who survives until the end.

00:06:24.880 --> 00:06:29.890
The prompt retreat at Kanegasaki, 
and this backing off now...

00:06:29.890 --> 00:06:33.120
Both will be the best way 
to protect your life.

00:06:34.090 --> 00:06:38.650
The enemy wants just 
one thing: your head.

00:06:38.650 --> 00:06:44.430
You took the great daimyo Imagawa down
 just by killing Yoshimoto.

00:06:44.430 --> 00:06:47.220
You of all people should know!

00:06:47.610 --> 00:06:50.370
Oh. Good point.

00:06:50.370 --> 00:06:52.850
I'm in Yoshimoto Imagawa's 
position right now.

00:06:53.390 --> 00:06:54.570
I see.

00:06:54.570 --> 00:06:56.270
Got it. I'll be careful.

00:07:03.080 --> 00:07:05.230
Nobunaga!

00:07:07.060 --> 00:07:08.990
Looks like they're coming.

00:07:08.990 --> 00:07:10.290
Retreat, my lord!

00:07:10.290 --> 00:07:11.690
To the back!

00:07:19.480 --> 00:07:22.710
Kazumasa Isono-sama 
cornered Nobunaga,

00:07:22.710 --> 00:07:24.500
but fell just one step short.

00:07:25.050 --> 00:07:27.660
Nobunaga is quick to get away.

00:07:29.400 --> 00:07:30.440
My lord,

00:07:30.440 --> 00:07:33.330
the Tokugawa army has 
defeated the Asakura army.

00:07:33.330 --> 00:07:34.860
They are fleeing!

00:07:34.860 --> 00:07:35.920
What?!

00:07:38.330 --> 00:07:42.910
The armies of Shibata, Niwa and Hashiba 
were scattered while attacking Yokoyama Castle,

00:07:42.910 --> 00:07:45.020
but they have returned 
to Oda's main army.

00:07:48.030 --> 00:07:48.960
My lord.

00:07:55.500 --> 00:07:57.950
Is that the man that took 
Naotsune Endo's life?

00:07:58.600 --> 00:08:02.830
But Endo is the highest 
chief retainer of the Asai family.

00:08:03.550 --> 00:08:05.330
I don't know yet.

00:08:05.330 --> 00:08:08.050
We will ask the 
surrendering Azai forces.

00:08:09.580 --> 00:08:11.420
Unwrap that head.

00:08:16.040 --> 00:08:16.550
Yes, sir.

00:08:31.320 --> 00:08:32.320
My lord!

00:08:32.540 --> 00:08:33.820
Are you okay?

00:08:38.330 --> 00:08:39.650
Who is that?

00:08:40.690 --> 00:08:42.340
Whose head is that?

00:08:42.920 --> 00:08:47.080
It's the head of the retainer 
Saemon Mitamura.

00:08:47.080 --> 00:08:52.840
He was heavily injured and 
barely breathing, so I ended his life.

00:08:54.090 --> 00:08:59.220
And why exactly did you sever 
the head of an ally?

00:09:01.740 --> 00:09:06.810
I will bring this head with me 
to Oda's main army.

00:09:08.040 --> 00:09:08.770
What?

00:09:09.260 --> 00:09:14.780
My lord, I did not come here 
to ask for your permission.

00:09:15.390 --> 00:09:19.560
I came simply to inform you

00:09:20.270 --> 00:09:22.870
that I will do what must be done.

00:09:25.560 --> 00:09:32.860
The only way Azai can defeat Oda 
is to take Nobunaga's head.

00:09:37.510 --> 00:09:42.500
<i>We are far from having Nobunaga's head,
aren't we, Naotsune?</i>

00:09:50.230 --> 00:09:52.270
Forgive me, Oichi.

00:09:52.270 --> 00:09:56.030
I could not bring you your gift.

00:09:58.330 --> 00:10:01.560
I told you. I don't want it.

00:10:12.210 --> 00:10:16.110
<i>About that time, on his way from Odani,
 Saburo visited Usayama Castle,</i>

00:10:16.110 --> 00:10:19.380
<i>which was being protected 
by Yoshinari Mori.</i>

00:10:19.840 --> 00:10:23.890
My lord, congratulations on your victory 
in the last battle.

00:10:24.290 --> 00:10:25.080
Sure.

00:10:25.730 --> 00:10:29.210
But I guess there's still 
going to be a lot more, huh?

00:10:29.730 --> 00:10:31.440
So I'm sorry, Yoshinari-san.

00:10:31.720 --> 00:10:32.650
Huh?

00:10:33.230 --> 00:10:35.300
I can't let you go home.

00:10:35.710 --> 00:10:37.190
You can't visit your kids, either.

00:10:37.700 --> 00:10:43.080
My lord, I thank you 
for such kind words.

00:10:43.600 --> 00:10:48.210
But I am grateful that you have 
chosen me to guard something

00:10:48.840 --> 00:10:50.580
as precious as Usayama.

00:10:51.260 --> 00:10:54.820
My sons have not even 
come of age yet.

00:10:54.820 --> 00:10:57.050
They are still children, and so 
they may not be useful in battle,

00:10:57.050 --> 00:11:00.430
but I would be very happy if 
you would be patient with them,

00:11:00.430 --> 00:11:02.300
and take good care of them.

00:11:14.130 --> 00:11:18.660
Having taken Yokoyama Castle 
in the previous battle

00:11:14.770 --> 00:11:16.050
<b>Miyoshi Three</b>

00:11:14.770 --> 00:11:16.050
<b>Noda Castle</b>

00:11:14.770 --> 00:11:16.050
<b>Fukushima Castle</b>

00:11:14.770 --> 00:11:19.850
<b>Yokoyama Castle</b>

00:11:14.770 --> 00:11:21.150
<b>Lake Biwa</b>

00:11:18.660 --> 00:11:21.900
and handed it over to Hideyoshi Hashiba 
and Hanbei Takenaka,

00:11:21.900 --> 00:11:26.790
Saburo himself traveled to Settsu 
to subjugate the Miysohi Three.

00:11:28.150 --> 00:11:29.880
Where's Nobunaga?

00:11:31.240 --> 00:11:34.610
Matsunaga-sama, please do not enter 
the main camp without permission!

00:11:34.610 --> 00:11:36.020
Let go of me, stupid!

00:11:36.350 --> 00:11:38.570
Hello, Matsunaga-san.

00:11:38.570 --> 00:11:41.160
It looks like you went ahead and 
fought the Miyoshi army for me.

00:11:41.160 --> 00:11:42.130
Thanks for that.

00:11:42.130 --> 00:11:43.920
It's such a pain in the ass.

00:11:43.920 --> 00:11:46.940
Miyoshi are wimps. You could 
have just wrecked them.

00:11:46.940 --> 00:11:49.480
What's the point of having 
tens of thousands of men?

00:11:49.480 --> 00:11:50.960
Gimme.

00:11:50.960 --> 00:11:51.730
Not gonna.

00:11:53.220 --> 00:11:54.900
Why is he displaying such attitude?

00:11:54.900 --> 00:11:58.390
That man has always had that 
attitude towards the lord.

00:11:58.390 --> 00:12:00.970
We all want to kill him,

00:12:00.970 --> 00:12:04.760
but we are restraining ourselves.

00:12:04.760 --> 00:12:06.040
But

00:12:06.040 --> 00:12:10.860
I am baffled by the way the lord

00:12:10.860 --> 00:12:12.900
seems to respect him somehow.

00:12:14.440 --> 00:12:17.410
Meanwhile in Oumi, 
at Yokoyama Castle...

00:12:17.950 --> 00:12:23.340
The Azai and Asakura forces have left 
the castle of Odani westward.

00:12:24.250 --> 00:12:25.670
Kyoto, huh.

00:12:27.640 --> 00:12:30.440
Alert the lord, quickly.

00:12:30.440 --> 00:12:30.850
Yes, sir!

00:12:31.860 --> 00:12:33.110
Sloppy.

00:12:33.810 --> 00:12:37.860
The only place to hold the west shore of 
Lake Biwa is at Usayama Castle.

00:12:38.690 --> 00:12:42.180
Mori-dono has roughly 
1,500 men for defense.

00:12:42.180 --> 00:12:44.530
The Asai and Asakura armies 
must have roughly 30,000.

00:12:45.330 --> 00:12:47.040
That is nowhere near enough.

00:12:48.370 --> 00:12:50.130
Say, Takenaka-dono.

00:12:50.960 --> 00:12:55.430
Miyoshi brings his forces 
to attract the Oda army to Settsu.

00:12:55.430 --> 00:12:59.500
Meanwhile, Asai and Asakura 
take Kyoto.

00:13:00.030 --> 00:13:02.340
Couldn't that be the plan?

00:13:02.340 --> 00:13:04.900
That is plausible.

00:13:04.900 --> 00:13:09.620
However, Miyoshi alone 
would not suffice.

00:13:10.720 --> 00:13:14.640
To attract Oda's massive army, 
there would need to be more.

00:13:15.390 --> 00:13:18.690
Do you suppose there's 
a larger army involved?

00:13:26.840 --> 00:13:29.040
Huh? What was that sound?

00:13:30.330 --> 00:13:32.470
Bells, perhaps?

00:13:33.090 --> 00:13:35.220
Temple bells?

00:13:35.220 --> 00:13:37.380
Why at such a time?

00:13:39.120 --> 00:13:41.550
I have received word that Ishiyama 
Hongan-ji has taken up arms.

00:13:42.390 --> 00:13:43.620
Say what?

00:13:44.390 --> 00:13:45.590
I bring news.

00:13:45.950 --> 00:13:48.540
Asai and Asakura are 
preparing to attack Kyoto.

00:13:48.540 --> 00:13:50.760
They're heading towards Usayama!

00:13:52.730 --> 00:13:56.730
My lord, we would not last for 
a moment if we fought them now.

00:13:57.180 --> 00:13:59.080
What do you plan to do?

00:13:59.080 --> 00:14:00.110
Calm down.

00:14:00.530 --> 00:14:02.340
Stop panicking.

00:14:02.870 --> 00:14:07.990
Our duty has not changed since 
we were handed Usayama Castle.

00:14:08.430 --> 00:14:12.660
Stop the enemies advancing from 
North Oumi, and protect Kyoto.

00:14:12.660 --> 00:14:16.660
The time has come for us 
to serve our purpose.

00:14:17.290 --> 00:14:20.300
But we are far outnumbered.

00:14:20.520 --> 00:14:23.440
We don't stand a proper chance!

00:14:23.440 --> 00:14:27.130
We don't need to fight them 
properly, do we?

00:14:29.150 --> 00:14:31.420
I leave you with 1,000 men.

00:14:31.420 --> 00:14:33.370
Protect this castle.

00:14:33.370 --> 00:14:37.210
I will take 500 men to 
ambush Asai and Asakura.

00:14:37.410 --> 00:14:40.100
You intend to leave 
the castle to fight?

00:14:40.100 --> 00:14:44.650
It is reckless to fight 
30,000 men with just 500.

00:14:44.650 --> 00:14:48.530
You will surely die 
in an open battle.

00:14:50.330 --> 00:14:53.380
I don't want to die, obviously.

00:14:53.380 --> 00:14:56.720
But I will do my job.

00:14:58.570 --> 00:15:01.470
The lord left me in charge 
of this crucial castle.

00:15:01.640 --> 00:15:03.800
I want to live up 
to his expectations.

00:15:05.300 --> 00:15:06.940
And more than anything,

00:15:08.990 --> 00:15:11.550
I want to make my sons proud.

00:15:12.320 --> 00:15:15.250
I would be an embarrassment to 
the Mori family if I wavered now.

00:15:19.070 --> 00:15:21.020
The Miyoshi Three.

00:15:21.020 --> 00:15:22.440
Ishiyama Hongan-ji.

00:15:23.020 --> 00:15:25.200
Asai and Asakura.

00:15:26.460 --> 00:15:28.740
Why have they all...?

00:15:29.260 --> 00:15:33.530
They are all cooperating to 
take down the Oda family.

00:15:35.780 --> 00:15:36.790
Micchi,

00:15:37.400 --> 00:15:39.950
go back to Kyoto and reinforce 
their defenses right away.

00:15:40.360 --> 00:15:42.930
Shibata-san, take care 
of the rear guard.

00:15:43.200 --> 00:15:44.960
Everyone else come with me.

00:15:46.160 --> 00:15:47.860
We're going to Usayama.

00:15:50.720 --> 00:15:52.350
Yo, Nobunaga.

00:15:53.700 --> 00:15:56.940
Looks like your luck's run out.

00:15:56.940 --> 00:15:57.970
I wonder.

00:16:01.930 --> 00:16:05.420
They are but a few hundred men!

00:16:05.420 --> 00:16:09.500
We don't have time to waste here!

00:16:09.500 --> 00:16:13.150
But the men at Usayama 
appear ready to die.

00:16:13.150 --> 00:16:14.780
They have terrifying morale.

00:16:14.780 --> 00:16:16.660
They are formidable.

00:16:17.320 --> 00:16:19.580
Especially the one with 
the cross spear.

00:16:19.580 --> 00:16:21.240
He's out of control!

00:16:24.100 --> 00:16:27.720
<i>How long has it been since 
I came to the Oda family?</i>

00:16:28.460 --> 00:16:30.840
<i>The young lord was famous 
for being a fool.</i>

00:16:30.840 --> 00:16:32.800
<i>But I learned that 
he would hire anyone,</i>

00:16:33.500 --> 00:16:37.170
<i>and so I, a wanderer, 
approached the Oda family.</i>

00:16:38.980 --> 00:16:40.140
All right!

00:16:40.140 --> 00:16:45.320
<i>Though Hirate-sama was quite upset 
that the lord was called a fool...</i>

00:16:45.730 --> 00:16:47.010
Mori-dono!

00:16:47.330 --> 00:16:48.630
Over there!

00:16:50.210 --> 00:16:52.500
Armed monks from Enryaku-ji.

00:16:52.500 --> 00:16:54.350
They're our enemies, too.

00:16:54.840 --> 00:16:57.240
We have even more enemies?

00:16:57.650 --> 00:16:59.390
We have only 500 men.

00:16:59.390 --> 00:17:01.840
30,000, 40,000, what 
difference does it make?

00:17:04.000 --> 00:17:05.370
Do not falter!

00:17:05.370 --> 00:17:08.170
Take down every enemy you see!

00:17:12.380 --> 00:17:15.960
<i>Hirate-sama, our lord 
was not at all a fool.</i>

00:17:15.960 --> 00:17:19.580
<i>He was in fact an incredible man.</i>

00:17:22.470 --> 00:17:23.440
<i>My lord.</i>

00:17:25.410 --> 00:17:27.470
<i>Have you made it to Kyoto?</i>

00:17:29.120 --> 00:17:30.960
It seems I am finally

00:17:32.970 --> 00:17:34.900
at my end.

00:17:46.790 --> 00:17:47.780
My lord,

00:17:49.070 --> 00:17:51.140
being able to serve you

00:17:52.690 --> 00:17:55.840
has been my greatest triumph.

00:17:59.790 --> 00:18:01.830
I pray

00:18:03.490 --> 00:18:06.960
that my sons will also aid you

00:18:07.940 --> 00:18:09.850
in your quest to take Japan.

00:18:41.940 --> 00:18:44.680
<i>When Saburo and his men 
arrived at the battlefield,</i>

00:18:46.250 --> 00:18:50.150
<i>there was not a single 
Oda soldier alive.</i>

00:18:51.050 --> 00:18:53.100
Excellent defense!

00:18:53.100 --> 00:18:56.900
It means a great deal that 
we have protected Usayama.

00:18:56.900 --> 00:18:57.690
Yes, sir!

00:18:58.500 --> 00:19:01.420
Mori-dono held them off well.

00:19:01.420 --> 00:19:04.060
It was clear to see 
on the battlefield.

00:19:04.060 --> 00:19:08.520
It was not only our 
men that were dead.

00:19:09.320 --> 00:19:14.670
With just 500 men, they killed that 
many Asai and Asakura soldiers.

00:19:15.100 --> 00:19:17.910
I can imagine Mori-dono fighting.

00:19:19.170 --> 00:19:22.060
My lord, Yoshinari Mori,

00:19:22.770 --> 00:19:24.920
must have thought of nothing

00:19:24.920 --> 00:19:27.920
but to keep the Asai and Asakura 
army from entering Kyoto.

00:19:28.640 --> 00:19:33.690
He must be glad that 
his wish has come true.

00:19:34.690 --> 00:19:35.650
My lord!

00:19:36.860 --> 00:19:39.610
We have found out where the 
Asai and Asakura armies are.

00:19:39.610 --> 00:19:41.810
They are at Mount Hiei.

00:19:41.810 --> 00:19:46.990
It appears that the Enryaku-ji monk soldiers 
have joined Asai Asakura in battle.

00:19:49.630 --> 00:19:51.800
First Hongan-ji, and now Enryaku-ji?

00:19:52.330 --> 00:19:53.300
Why?

00:19:53.780 --> 00:19:58.330
Is it a thing now for 
monks to oppose me?

00:20:03.580 --> 00:20:07.180
Go back to Gifu and 
tell the Mori brothers:

00:20:08.190 --> 00:20:12.530
I'll take care of them 
in place of their father.

00:20:31.050 --> 00:20:33.120
My brother is crying.

00:20:34.130 --> 00:20:36.320
Is it a sign of impending disaster?

00:20:41.530 --> 00:20:42.670
Father.

00:20:42.990 --> 00:20:45.130
Is the war over?

00:20:50.040 --> 00:20:51.140
Ranmaru.

00:20:52.360 --> 00:20:53.450
Ranmaru.

00:20:54.580 --> 00:20:55.980
Ranmaru!

00:20:59.210 --> 00:21:02.230
Starting today, I am 
the head of this house.

00:21:03.220 --> 00:21:04.530
Understand?

00:21:15.960 --> 00:21:17.320
Father...
